# The scan counts every store into what `super()` answers as a part of the construction. A constructor above may answer with another object than the one that this construction makes:
# then `new B(2)` stores into the object that `new B(1)` made, and `x` is written long behind its making. Where every constructor above answers with its own object, `y` is written at the construction alone
